"""
Wrist-driven strum demo for the Prostheticasters right (strumming) hand.

This replaces the old chord-pose demo (open/C_chord/G_chord/power_strum/pinch),
which was left over from last year's fretting-hand team and cycled static hand
SHAPES rather than showing a strum. This semester's sim needs to:
  1. Be tied to a hand model that actually has a thumb and functional wrist
     joints. We load right_hand.xml, which has the full wrist_PRO /
     wrist_UDEV / wrist_FLEX chain plus a complete thumb.
  2. Demonstrate STRUMMING specifically: a wrist sweep across the strings
     over time, with a pick held in a fixed grip, timed to a tempo/song --
     not a sequence of static fretting-style chord shapes.
  3. Reuse the hand-agnostic timing engine from Parsing/GuitarProReader.py
     when a real song is available.

Run from the repo root (CapstoneBioGuitar-main/):
    python Sim\\mvmnt_demo.py        (Windows)
    python3 Sim/mvmnt_demo.py        (Linux/Mac)

CALIBRATE MODE:
Set CALIBRATE = True to get live sliders (hand x/y/z + roll/pitch/yaw, guitar
x/y/z) in the PyBullet GUI for lining the hand up with the guitar, with
ready-to-paste values printed to the terminal once a second. HAND_ANCHOR_POS /
HAND_ANCHOR_EULER_DEG / GUITAR_POS below are Jimmy's tuned values from
2026-09-10 -- CALIBRATE defaults to False now that those are in place.
Flip it back to True any time the position needs more adjustment.

STRUM TIMING MODEL:
Each played NOTE gets a quick, fixed-length flick -- not a slow interpolation
that stretches across however long you then wait. Rests and held notes just
extend the wait between flicks; nothing moves during that wait. This is why
a rest doesn't look like slow motion, and a run of fast notes looks like a
run of fast, distinct strikes. The (waited X.XXs) printed for every strum
is the real gap pulled straight from the song's note onset times, so you
can eyeball whether the motion is landing in time with the tempo.

STRUM DIRECTIONS:
STRUM_DIRECTIONS below is the pattern of strokes to cycle through --
["D", "U"] for normal alternating strumming, or ["D"] for down-strokes
only (any custom pattern works too, e.g. ["D", "D", "U"]).

STRUM MOTION MODEL (wrist only, for now):
wrist_UDEV (the wrist's own yaw) is the actual strum sweep across the
strings; wrist_FLEX is only ever used as a clearance lift, and only when
needed (see below). Each stroke looks at what the NEXT stroke in
STRUM_DIRECTIONS will be:
  - If the next stroke is the OPPOSITE direction (the normal alternating
    case): this stroke is a single continuous sweep from wherever the
    wrist currently sits to its own target, and it just HOLDS there --
    it does not sweep back to neutral on its own. The *next* stroke's
    sweep is what carries the wrist back across the strings to the
    opposite extreme -- that crossing is a real, intentional strike (the
    next note), not a spurious extra one. This is what keeps a stroke
    from re-catching the strings on a "return" trip: there is no separate
    return trip, so nothing to accidentally re-strike with.
  - If the next stroke is the SAME direction (e.g. down-strokes-only
    patterns, where nothing else is ever going to sweep the wrist back):
    this stroke does its own out-and-back within its single
    STRIKE_DURATION -- sweep out to the target, lift clear via wrist_FLEX,
    swing back to neutral while still lifted, then settle the lift back
    down -- so its own return trip doesn't drag back through the strings
    it just struck. This is the same idea as the very first fix for the
    "catches the strings" problem, just now applied only where it's
    actually needed instead of on every stroke.
The anchor/forearm is welded at Jimmy's calibrated position and does not
move during the strum -- an earlier version also animated the anchor's yaw
to mimic forearm rotation, but that's parked for now in favor of wrist-only
motion.
"""

import math
import os
import sys
from time import perf_counter, sleep

import pybullet as pb
import pybullet_data

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Config
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

HAND_MODEL_PATH = "Sim/MPL/right_hand.xml"   # full thumb + 3-DOF wrist model

CALIBRATE = False   # set True to get position/rotation sliders again

HAND_ANCHOR_POS = [0.411, 0.000, 0.537]                # Jimmy's tuned anchor position, 2026-09-10
HAND_ANCHOR_EULER_DEG = [-13.263, -18.947, -123.158]   # Jimmy's tuned anchor roll/pitch/yaw, 2026-09-10
GUITAR_POS = [-0.375, -0.268, 0.468]                   # Jimmy's tuned guitar position, 2026-09-10

BPM = 90.0                                     # fallback tempo if no song file is loaded
# SONG_FILE = "Parsing/inputs/Apollo-Live.gp3"   # set to None to always use the BPM fallback instead
SONG_FILE = None   # set to None to always use the BPM fallback instead
SONG_TRACK = 0

STRUM_DIRECTIONS = ["D"]   # stroke pattern to cycle through -- ["D", "U"] for normal
                            # alternating strumming, ["D"] for down-strokes only, or any
                            # custom sequence (e.g. ["D", "D", "U"]). See module docstring.

STRIKE_DURATION = 0.15   # seconds -- how long a single stroke's sweep to its target takes
                          # (or, for a same-direction-repeat stroke, its whole out-and-back)

# wrist_UDEV (the wrist's own yaw) -- the actual strum sweep across the
# strings. Real joint range is roughly -14.9..45 deg, NOT symmetric, so
# these two are deliberately different magnitudes. Each stroke sweeps to
# ONE of these -- see STRUM MOTION MODEL above.
WRIST_YAW_DOWN_DEG = -20.0
WRIST_YAW_UP_DEG = 25.0

# wrist_FLEX (pitch) -- used ONLY as a clearance lift for a stroke that has
# to return to neutral on its own (see STRUM MOTION MODEL above). Real
# joint range is roughly -59.6..59.6 deg. If this makes the hand dip INTO
# the guitar instead of lifting away, flip the sign -- you'll see it
# immediately.
LIFT_FLEX_DEG = 20.0

# Phase boundaries (fractions of STRIKE_DURATION) for a stroke that has to
# return to neutral on its own: 0 -> STRIKE_OUT_FRAC sweeps out to target;
# that -> STRIKE_LIFT_FRAC lifts clear (wrist_FLEX) while still holding the
# yaw out; that -> STRIKE_RETURN_FRAC swings the yaw back to neutral while
# still lifted; that -> 1.0 settles the lift back down. Keep
# 0 < STRIKE_OUT_FRAC < STRIKE_LIFT_FRAC < STRIKE_RETURN_FRAC < 1.0.
# Unused for a stroke whose next stroke is the opposite direction.
STRIKE_OUT_FRAC = 0.40
STRIKE_LIFT_FRAC = 0.55
STRIKE_RETURN_FRAC = 0.80

WRIST_PRO_BASE_DEG = 0.0  # constant forearm rotation aiming the hand over the strings

STRING_LINK_NAMES = {f"string{i}" for i in range(1, 7)}
CONTACT_LINK_HINTS = ("thumb", "index", "middle", "ring", "pinky")  # fingertip-ish links we care about for contact logging


def d(deg):
    return deg * math.pi / 180.0


def smooth_step(t):
    """Ease-in-out curve: starts/ends slow, fast in the middle."""
    t = max(0.0, min(1.0, t))
    return t * t * (3 - 2 * t)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Strum timeline: a list of (direction, gap_before_this_note) pairs, where
# gap_before is the real-world time to WAIT (holding still, no motion)
# before firing the next quick strike. Either driven by a real song via
# GuitarProReader (rests skipped entirely -- they just lengthen the gap
# before the next played note), or a simple constant-tempo metronome
# pattern as a no-dependency fallback. Direction comes from STRUM_DIRECTIONS,
# cycled in order.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def build_strum_events_from_song(song_path, track=0):
    """Returns a list of (direction, gap_before_seconds) for each PLAYED
    note (rests are skipped, not turned into their own slow motion --
    they just add to the gap before the next real note). direction cycles
    through STRUM_DIRECTIONS per note.
    Returns None if the song can't be loaded/parsed so callers can fall back."""
    try:
        sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), "..", "Parsing"))
        from GuitarProReader import GuitarProSong
    except Exception as e:
        print(f"[strum] Couldn't import GuitarProReader ({e}); using fallback metronome pattern.")
        return None

    if not song_path or not os.path.exists(song_path):
        print(f"[strum] SONG_FILE not found ({song_path}); using fallback metronome pattern.")
        return None

    try:
        song = GuitarProSong(song_path)
        onsets = []  # (direction, absolute_time) for every beat that actually has notes
        i = 0
        for timed_measure in song.yield_timed_measures(track):
            for timed_beat in timed_measure.yield_timed_beats():
                if not timed_beat.beat.notes:
                    continue  # rest: no strike, it just lengthens the gap before the next one
                onsets.append((STRUM_DIRECTIONS[i % len(STRUM_DIRECTIONS)], timed_beat.time))
                i += 1

        if not onsets:
            print("[strum] Song loaded but had no played notes (all rests?); using fallback metronome pattern.")
            return None

        events = []
        prev_time = onsets[0][1]
        for idx, (direction, t) in enumerate(onsets):
            gap = 0.0 if idx == 0 else max(0.0, t - prev_time)
            events.append((direction, gap))
            prev_time = t

        print(f"[strum] Loaded {len(events)} played-note strum events (rests skipped) from {song_path}")
        return events
    except Exception as e:
        print(f"[strum] Failed to parse {song_path} ({e}); using fallback metronome pattern.")
        return None


def build_fallback_strum_events(bpm, n_events=64):
    """Eighth-note pattern at a constant tempo, cycling through STRUM_DIRECTIONS."""
    eighth_note_seconds = 60.0 / bpm / 2.0
    return [(STRUM_DIRECTIONS[i % len(STRUM_DIRECTIONS)], eighth_note_seconds) for i in range(n_events)]


_song_events = build_strum_events_from_song(SONG_FILE, SONG_TRACK) if SONG_FILE else None
STRUM_EVENTS = _song_events if _song_events is not None else build_fallback_strum_events(BPM)
TEMPO_SOURCE = "song file" if _song_events is not None else f"{BPM} BPM fallback"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hand shape: a clenched-ish fist, mimicking a pick loosely held in the
# closed hand. Placeholder until we model an actual pick + a precise
# thumb/index pinch grip -- for now this is just meant to look like a fist
# wrapped around something, not an open hand.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GRIP_POSE = {
    "wrist_PRO": d(WRIST_PRO_BASE_DEG),
    "thumb_ABD": d(15), "thumb_MCP": d(45), "thumb_PIP": d(55), "thumb_DIP": d(35),
    "index_MCP": d(70), "index_PIP": d(95), "index_DIP": d(60),
    "middle_MCP": d(75), "middle_PIP": d(100), "middle_DIP": d(65),
    "ring_MCP": d(75), "ring_PIP": d(100), "ring_DIP": d(65),
    "pinky_MCP": d(75), "pinky_PIP": d(100), "pinky_DIP": d(65),
}


def strike_pose(direction, phase, start_udev, return_to_neutral):
    """See module docstring (STRUM MOTION MODEL).

    return_to_neutral=False (next stroke is the opposite direction): a
    single continuous sweep from start_udev to this stroke's target,
    holding there once reached -- the next stroke does the return.

    return_to_neutral=True (next stroke is the same direction, e.g.
    down-only patterns): this stroke's own out-and-back --
    STRIKE / LIFT / RETURN / SETTLE -- so it clears the strings on its own
    return trip instead of dragging back through them."""
    pose = dict(GRIP_POSE)
    target = d(WRIST_YAW_DOWN_DEG if direction == "D" else WRIST_YAW_UP_DEG)

    if not return_to_neutral:
        t = smooth_step(phase)
        pose["wrist_UDEV"] = start_udev + (target - start_udev) * t
        pose["wrist_FLEX"] = 0.0
        return pose

    lift_target = d(LIFT_FLEX_DEG)
    if phase <= STRIKE_OUT_FRAC:
        # STRIKE: sweep out to the target, no lift yet.
        t = smooth_step(phase / STRIKE_OUT_FRAC) if STRIKE_OUT_FRAC > 0 else 1.0
        pose["wrist_UDEV"] = start_udev + (target - start_udev) * t
        pose["wrist_FLEX"] = 0.0
    elif phase <= STRIKE_LIFT_FRAC:
        # LIFT: rise clear of the strings while still holding the yaw out.
        span = STRIKE_LIFT_FRAC - STRIKE_OUT_FRAC
        t = smooth_step((phase - STRIKE_OUT_FRAC) / span) if span > 0 else 1.0
        pose["wrist_UDEV"] = target
        pose["wrist_FLEX"] = lift_target * t
    elif phase <= STRIKE_RETURN_FRAC:
        # RETURN: swing yaw back to neutral while still lifted clear.
        span = STRIKE_RETURN_FRAC - STRIKE_LIFT_FRAC
        t = smooth_step((phase - STRIKE_LIFT_FRAC) / span) if span > 0 else 1.0
        pose["wrist_UDEV"] = target * (1 - t)
        pose["wrist_FLEX"] = lift_target
    else:
        # SETTLE: lower back down to neutral, ready for the next strike.
        span = 1.0 - STRIKE_RETURN_FRAC
        t = smooth_step((phase - STRIKE_RETURN_FRAC) / span) if span > 0 else 1.0
        pose["wrist_UDEV"] = 0.0
        pose["wrist_FLEX"] = lift_target * (1 - t)
    return pose


def hold_pose(udev):
    """Pose for the wait/no-motion portion of an event: grip held still at
    whichever wrist_UDEV angle the last stroke stopped at (neutral if that
    stroke returned to neutral on its own -- see module docstring)."""
    pose = dict(GRIP_POSE)
    pose["wrist_UDEV"] = udev
    pose["wrist_FLEX"] = 0.0
    return pose


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PyBullet setup
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

physicsClient = pb.connect(pb.GUI)
pb.setGravity(0, 0, -9.81)
pb.setAdditionalSearchPath(pybullet_data.getDataPath())
pb.loadURDF("plane.urdf")

models = pb.loadMJCF(HAND_MODEL_PATH)
hand = models[0]

for i in range(-1, pb.getNumJoints(hand)):
    pb.changeDynamics(hand, i, collisionMargin=0.00001)

guitar_parts = pb.loadURDF(
    "Sim/guitar_model/guitar.urdf",
    basePosition=GUITAR_POS,
    baseOrientation=pb.getQuaternionFromEuler([0, 0, math.pi / 2]),
    useFixedBase=True
)

pb.setPhysicsEngineParameter(
    numSolverIterations=200,
    numSubSteps=4,
    contactBreakingThreshold=0.00001,
    enableConeFriction=1
)
pb.setTimeStep(1 / 240)

constraint = pb.createConstraint(
    parentBodyUniqueId=hand,
    parentLinkIndex=-1,
    childBodyUniqueId=-1,
    childLinkIndex=-1,
    jointType=pb.JOINT_FIXED,
    jointAxis=[0, 0, 0],
    parentFramePosition=[0, 0, 0],
    childFramePosition=HAND_ANCHOR_POS,
    childFrameOrientation=pb.getQuaternionFromEuler([d(a) for a in HAND_ANCHOR_EULER_DEG])
)

pb.resetDebugVisualizerCamera(
    cameraDistance=0.5, cameraYaw=45,
    cameraPitch=-20, cameraTargetPosition=[0, 0, 0.55]
)

name_index = {}
for i in range(pb.getNumJoints(hand)):
    info = pb.getJointInfo(hand, i)
    if info[2] != pb.JOINT_FIXED:
        name_index[info[1].decode()] = i

# Guardrail: catch a future accidental revert to a thumb-less / wrist-less
# model early with a clear message instead of silently doing nothing, since
# that's exactly the bug this rewrite fixes.
_required = {"wrist_PRO", "wrist_UDEV", "wrist_FLEX", "thumb_ABD", "thumb_MCP"}
_missing = _required - set(name_index.keys())
if _missing:
    raise RuntimeError(
        f"Loaded hand model '{HAND_MODEL_PATH}' is missing joints {sorted(_missing)}. "
        "This demo needs a model with a full wrist (PRO/UDEV/FLEX) and a thumb -- "
        "MPL.xml does not have a thumb; use right_hand.xml or mpl2.xml instead."
    )

# Precompute which link indices belong to the guitar's 6 strings, and which
# hand link indices look like fingertip/thumb links, so contact logging can
# report something readable (e.g. "down-strum hit string3, string4") instead
# of a raw per-timestep dump of every contact pair.
guitar_link_names = {-1: "base"}
for i in range(pb.getNumJoints(guitar_parts)):
    guitar_link_names[i] = pb.getJointInfo(guitar_parts, i)[1].decode()
string_link_indices = {i for i, n in guitar_link_names.items() if n in STRING_LINK_NAMES}

hand_link_names = {-1: "base"}
for i in range(pb.getNumJoints(hand)):
    hand_link_names[i] = pb.getJointInfo(hand, i)[1].decode()


def apply_pose(pose):
    for name, idx in name_index.items():
        target = pose.get(name, 0.0)
        pb.setJointMotorControl2(
            bodyUniqueId=hand,
            jointIndex=idx,
            controlMode=pb.POSITION_CONTROL,
            targetPosition=target,
            force=10
        )


dt = 1 / 240

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CALIBRATE mode: freeze the hand in its neutral grip pose and expose the
# anchor position/rotation and guitar position as live sliders, so you can
# drag them into alignment by eye instead of guessing numbers blind.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

if CALIBRATE:
    sliders = {
        "anchor_x": pb.addUserDebugParameter("anchor_x", -1.0, 1.0, HAND_ANCHOR_POS[0]),
        "anchor_y": pb.addUserDebugParameter("anchor_y", -1.0, 1.0, HAND_ANCHOR_POS[1]),
        "anchor_z": pb.addUserDebugParameter("anchor_z", -1.0, 1.0, HAND_ANCHOR_POS[2]),
        "anchor_roll": pb.addUserDebugParameter("anchor_roll_deg", -180, 180, HAND_ANCHOR_EULER_DEG[0]),
        "anchor_pitch": pb.addUserDebugParameter("anchor_pitch_deg", -180, 180, HAND_ANCHOR_EULER_DEG[1]),
        "anchor_yaw": pb.addUserDebugParameter("anchor_yaw_deg", -180, 180, HAND_ANCHOR_EULER_DEG[2]),
        "guitar_x": pb.addUserDebugParameter("guitar_x", -1.5, 1.5, GUITAR_POS[0]),
        "guitar_y": pb.addUserDebugParameter("guitar_y", -1.5, 1.5, GUITAR_POS[1]),
        "guitar_z": pb.addUserDebugParameter("guitar_z", -1.0, 1.0, GUITAR_POS[2]),
    }
    guitar_orn = pb.getQuaternionFromEuler([0, 0, math.pi / 2])
    print("[calibrate] Drag the sliders in the GUI until the hand sits naturally over the "
          "strings. Current values print here once a second -- copy the final ones into "
          "HAND_ANCHOR_POS / HAND_ANCHOR_EULER_DEG / GUITAR_POS at the top of this file, "
          "then set CALIBRATE = False.")

    print_timer = 0.0
    next_tick = perf_counter()
    while True:
        ax = pb.readUserDebugParameter(sliders["anchor_x"])
        ay = pb.readUserDebugParameter(sliders["anchor_y"])
        az = pb.readUserDebugParameter(sliders["anchor_z"])
        roll = pb.readUserDebugParameter(sliders["anchor_roll"])
        pitch = pb.readUserDebugParameter(sliders["anchor_pitch"])
        yaw = pb.readUserDebugParameter(sliders["anchor_yaw"])
        gx = pb.readUserDebugParameter(sliders["guitar_x"])
        gy = pb.readUserDebugParameter(sliders["guitar_y"])
        gz = pb.readUserDebugParameter(sliders["guitar_z"])

        pb.changeConstraint(
            constraint,
            jointChildPivot=[ax, ay, az],
            jointChildFrameOrientation=pb.getQuaternionFromEuler([d(roll), d(pitch), d(yaw)]),
            maxForce=500
        )
        pb.resetBasePositionAndOrientation(guitar_parts, [gx, gy, gz], guitar_orn)
        apply_pose(GRIP_POSE)

        pb.stepSimulation()

        print_timer += dt
        if print_timer >= 1.0:
            print_timer = 0.0
            print(f"HAND_ANCHOR_POS = [{ax:.3f}, {ay:.3f}, {az:.3f}]   "
                  f"HAND_ANCHOR_EULER_DEG = [{roll:.1f}, {pitch:.1f}, {yaw:.1f}]   "
                  f"GUITAR_POS = [{gx:.3f}, {gy:.3f}, {gz:.3f}]")

        # Pace to wall-clock dt instead of always sleeping a full dt on top
        # of however long this iteration's work took -- see main loop below
        # for why that matters.
        next_tick += dt
        now = perf_counter()
        if next_tick > now:
            sleep(next_tick - now)
        else:
            next_tick = now  # fell behind -- resync instead of stacking up lag

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Normal mode: walk the strum timeline. Each event is (direction, gap) --
# gap seconds of holding still (no motion, wherever the last stroke left
# off), then a fixed STRIKE_DURATION motion to this stroke's target (see
# module docstring for whether that's a one-way sweep-and-hold or a full
# out-and-back, depending on what the NEXT stroke's direction is).
# Rests/long notes just make gap bigger; they never slow the strike itself
# down. The forearm/anchor stays fixed the whole time.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

event_idx = 0
event_elapsed = 0.0
strings_hit_this_stroke = set()
held_udev = 0.0  # wherever the wrist is currently resting -- starts at neutral, then
                  # becomes wherever each stroke's own motion stops once that stroke finishes

# --- diagnostics for the "starts on time, bogs down after N strikes" investigation ---
# Per event: real wall-clock seconds actually spent (vs. the fixed sim-time
# budget it was allotted), the max simultaneous hand<->guitar contact count
# seen, and whether any contact showed up during the LIFT/RETURN clearance
# window -- the phase where the hand is supposed to be lifted clear of the
# strings on its own return trip. If LIFT_FLEX_DEG's sign is wrong, this is
# exactly where it will show up, and if the hand is embedding deeper into
# the strings strike after strike, event_wall_seconds and max_contacts
# should visibly climb starting at whichever strike # things go bad.
event_wall_start = perf_counter()
event_max_contacts = 0
event_clearance_violations = 0

print(f"[strum] {len(STRUM_EVENTS)} events queued, tempo source: {TEMPO_SOURCE}, "
      f"directions: {STRUM_DIRECTIONS}")

# Pace the loop to wall-clock dt rather than always sleeping a full dt
# after each iteration. sleep(dt) unconditionally means real time per loop
# is (however long stepSimulation/contact-checking/etc. actually took) +
# dt -- if that work takes, say, 4x dt, the whole sim runs 5x slower than
# real time even though every physics step is still exactly dt of
# simulated time. Tracking next_tick and sleeping only the REMAINING time
# keeps it paced to real time whenever the machine can keep up, and just
# free-runs (no sleep) instead of compounding delay when it can't.
next_tick = perf_counter()
while True:
    direction, gap = STRUM_EVENTS[event_idx % len(STRUM_EVENTS)]
    next_direction, _ = STRUM_EVENTS[(event_idx + 1) % len(STRUM_EVENTS)]
    return_to_neutral = (next_direction == direction)  # nothing else will sweep this stroke back

    strike_time = min(STRIKE_DURATION, gap) if gap > 0 else STRIKE_DURATION
    wait_time = max(0.0, gap - strike_time)
    total_event_time = wait_time + strike_time

    if event_elapsed < wait_time:
        apply_pose(hold_pose(held_udev))  # holding still at wherever the last stroke stopped
        phase = None
    else:
        phase = (event_elapsed - wait_time) / strike_time if strike_time > 0 else 1.0
        apply_pose(strike_pose(direction, phase, held_udev, return_to_neutral))

    pb.stepSimulation()

    contacts = pb.getContactPoints(hand, guitar_parts)
    event_max_contacts = max(event_max_contacts, len(contacts))
    if (
        phase is not None and return_to_neutral
        and STRIKE_LIFT_FRAC <= phase <= STRIKE_RETURN_FRAC
        and contacts
    ):
        event_clearance_violations += 1

    for c in contacts:
        h_link, g_link = c[3], c[4]
        if g_link in string_link_indices and any(hint in hand_link_names.get(h_link, "") for hint in CONTACT_LINK_HINTS):
            strings_hit_this_stroke.add(guitar_link_names[g_link])

    event_elapsed += dt
    if event_elapsed >= total_event_time:
        event_wall_seconds = perf_counter() - event_wall_start
        arrow = "↓" if direction == "D" else "↑"
        hit_str = ", ".join(sorted(strings_hit_this_stroke)) if strings_hit_this_stroke else "(no string contact)"
        print(f"{arrow} strum #{event_idx} (waited {wait_time:.2f}s, took {event_wall_seconds:.3f}s real time, "
              f"max_contacts={event_max_contacts}): {hit_str}")
        if event_clearance_violations:
            print(f"    ERROR: contact during {event_clearance_violations} LIFT/RETURN clearance step(s) -- "
                  f"LIFT_FLEX_DEG may have the wrong sign (hand isn't actually clearing the strings on return)")
        target = d(WRIST_YAW_DOWN_DEG if direction == "D" else WRIST_YAW_UP_DEG)
        held_udev = 0.0 if return_to_neutral else target  # wherever this stroke's own motion actually stopped
        strings_hit_this_stroke = set()
        event_elapsed = 0.0
        event_idx += 1
        event_wall_start = perf_counter()
        event_max_contacts = 0
        event_clearance_violations = 0

    next_tick += dt
    now = perf_counter()
    if next_tick > now:
        sleep(next_tick - now)
    else:
        next_tick = now  # fell behind -- resync instead of stacking up lag
